## Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose. For example, personal use, research, experimentation, personal study, private entertainment, hobby projects, amateur pursuits, and religious observance are all permitted purposes.

## Commercial Purposes

Commercial purposes are not permitted purposes. For example, using the software to provide a service for which you charge, using the software in your business, or using the software in the course of your employment are all commercial purposes.

## Fair Use

You may have "fair use" rights for the software under the law. These terms do not limit them.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not allow you to sublicense or transfer any of your licenses to anyone else, or to prevent the licensor from granting licenses to anyone else. These terms do not give you any other rights.

